NAME
    writers - find static write references to an address

SYNOPSIS
    writers [<space>] <addr> [<scanstart> <scanlen>] [--json]

DESCRIPTION
    Scans CpuBus (or the named processor's code space when <space> is
    given) for instructions that statically store to hex address <addr>.
    By default the scan covers <addr>'s own bank from $8000 to $FFFF;
    supply hex <scanstart> and <scanlen> to scan another range.

    Only statically encoded addressing modes on systems with a static
    disassembler are detected. When static disassembly is unavailable or
    when writes use indexed or indirect addressing, --json reports
    "supported": false with runtime watch(1) guidance; use 'watch add'
    and 'watch summary' for runtime write detection across all consoles.

EXAMPLES
    writers 13c6
    writers WRAM 007E --json
    writers 13c6 808000 8000

EXIT STATUS
    0   Scan completed (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, invalid hex argument, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    readers(1), callers(1), watch(1), bp(1), disasm(1)
